Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 04:27:43 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] IOSV-FORMSHOW / IOSV-SHOWALL / HSYS-EVT: compK ioS -- the IO
 page's golden FormShow from C++, chkShowIndexAll, HandlerSys click replays

* FileRW/IoSetViewFormShow_File.cpp (new, S12 second-type bridge, display only): golden Tfiosetview::FormShow's screen half
  (iosetview.cpp:236-1023 + ShowSuckMode :1313, ShowShuttleSensor :1671, LabSiteMap :2861, Hide_1032_IO :3907; labUseSensor1/2
  from cinitial.cpp:15012-15047), served as GET /api/form/HW.IoSetView.html. Machine outputs, card reads, engine state and the
  login locks (EastSun 20260929: no locks on the IO page) are NOT copied -- each listed in the file header. One form.event:
  chkShowIndexAll click = golden chkShowIndexAllClick :1760-1766 (ShowSuckMode(-1): colours / captions only).
* FileRW/_registry.cpp / _formbridge_sources.cmake: register kBridge_Tfiosetview.
* FileRW/HSys.cpp BeforeApply: also replays golden rgTTLCardClick (906 HandlerSys.cpp:1246-1255) and rgRotateKit_TypeClick
  (:1132-1136) before non-editable values are dropped, so a value the click re-enables is saved as golden saves it.
* tests: test_iosetview_formshow_bridge (ctest IoSetViewFormShowBridge, 35 checks: this machine's config, a second config, the
  form.event) and test_hsys_heater_mix CaseTTLRotateReplay (ctest HSys_HeaterMix, 149 checks).

Nothing is sent to the machine; the tests read and write no machine file.
